## Inventory Log

Written by `/kaizen-update-docs`: one line per day an inventory was made, newest first, three days at most. A promotion candidate that has no entry (one that comes from auto memory, for example) is also placed here. The format is under "Markers" below.

(No inventory yet)

## Entry Format

```markdown
### [Short title] (YYYY-MM-DD)

- **Situation**: What you were trying to do
- **Problem**: What went wrong or what constraint was discovered
- **Lesson**: What to do differently next time
- **Promotion candidate**: One line on why it belongs in knowledge/  <!-- optional: it should be in knowledge/ and is not yet -->
- **Promoted**: → knowledge/path.md § Section  <!-- optional: once promoted, the candidate line becomes this -->
```

## Markers

Read by the label at the start of the line (`kaizen-learnings-inventory.sh`). Do not change the labels.

| Line | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `- **Promotion candidate**: <why>` | It should be in `knowledge/` and is not yet. The next `/kaizen-reflect-learning` receives it |
| `- **Promotion candidate**: <why> (deferred until: <condition>)` | Not handed over now. Reviewed again when the condition occurs |
| `- **Promoted**: → knowledge/<path>.md § <section>` | Promoted. The cross-project audit of `/kaizen-audit-knowledge` skips the entry |
| `- **Inventory**: YYYY-MM-DD (knowledge@<commit>) — <result>` | The record of an inventory (written in the section above). `knowledge@<commit>` is what the next inventory narrows its scope from |

